// E0208: a `derive` outside the module declaring its target.
//
// The orphan rule, and it is the cheapest coherence available. Without it two
// modules can each derive for one type and produce two *names* for one canonical
// encoding — and with explicit dictionaries nothing at a call site says which
// one it got, so the same type serializes two ways and no one notices until a
// client breaks. With it, "one canonical dictionary per type" is a local
// property, checkable from what a module can see.
//
// The fix is to move the `derive` next to the `type`, which is also where a
// change to the type will be.

import users

derive eq for User
